  "reasoning": [
    "The private final monitor serializes observations on one adapter. The monitor spans context authentication, manager projections, repeated kernel namespace checks and verification before return. The method does blocking observation under this monitor.",
    "Per-instance serialization is required to be preserved if the locking mechanism changes. The monitor does not serialize other adapters or processes. Separate ownership, manager/kernel observations, M/A where applicable, and fail-closed outcomes remain in the scope of SS341 and SS343.",
    "The interrupt checks run after acquisition and around observation. Waiting for synchronized acquisition itself has no interrupt or deadline contract. BTERM006 has synthetic interruption positions and shared/unshared instances, but its source does not control acquisition order or show deadline while another call already holds the lock.",
    "PMD applicability does not by itself establish a production contract violation or mandate a specific replacement. Static zero, any disposition, and authorized evidence are still required by 451."
  ],
